<section class="section-dark">
<div class="wrap">
<div class="grid-head reveal">
<h2 class="h2">Questions about MIA transfers</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
</div>
<div class="faq reveal">
<details><summary>Where exactly at MIA do you meet arriving passengers?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Curbside at the arrivals level by default, or a meet-and-greet point just past baggage claim if you'd rather not manage bags to the curb alone — confirmed with you when you book, not decided on the day.</div></details>
<details><summary>What happens if my flight is delayed or lands early?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Your chauffeur tracks the flight in real time and adjusts the pickup window automatically. Early or late, the fixed quote you were given at booking doesn't change.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do you serve MIA for connecting cruise passengers?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Yes. MIA-to-PortMiami and MIA-to-Port Everglades transfers are booked the same way as any airport run, timed against your ship's boarding window rather than a generic drive-time estimate.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is there room for golf clubs or extra luggage from MIA?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">The Suburban RST seats up to six with luggage capacity confirmed before booking based on passenger count, bag count, and anything oversized like golf clubs or strollers.</div></details>
<details><summary>Can I book a one-way MIA transfer and a separate return later?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Yes. Most bookings are one-way pickups or drop-offs; round-trip and standing return dates are arranged just as easily on the same fixed-quote basis.</div></details>
</div>
</div>
